 "title": "Identities never cross brands",
 "description": "Each brand's users, sessions, organizations, and app passwords exist only within that brand. A session or app password from one brand is rejected by every other brand, and the same email registered at two brands is two separate users.",
 "traces_to": "intent.direction.proposals[2] -- SHALL because a settled proposal",
 "verification": {
  "acceptance": [
   "A session from brand A presented to brand B is not accepted",
   "An app password from brand A does not authenticate at brand B",
   "The same email at two brands produces two different user ids"
  ],
  "criteria": [
   {
    "text": "A session from brand A presented to brand B is not accepted",
    "id": "01a11359-7d9c-7f40-b83a-4a74ba72a7b2"
   },
   {
    "text": "An app password from brand A does not authenticate at brand B",
    "id": "01a11359-7d9c-7f40-b83a-4a86b453e8ea"
   },
   {
    "text": "The same email at two brands produces two different user ids",
    "id": "01a11359-7d9c-7f40-b83a-4a935accbbc7"
   }
  ],
  "scenarios": [
   {
    "criterion_id": "01a11359-7d9c-7f40-b83a-4a74ba72a7b2",
    "gherkin": "@criterion-01a11359-7d9c-7f40-b83a-4a74ba72a7b2\nScenario: A session from one brand is not accepted by another brand\n  Given a user signed in at brand A with a valid session\n  When that session is presented to brand B\n  Then brand B does not accept the session"
   },
   {
    "criterion_id": "01a11359-7d9c-7f40-b83a-4a86b453e8ea",
    "gherkin": "@criterion-01a11359-7d9c-7f40-b83a-4a86b453e8ea\nScenario: An app password from one brand does not authenticate at another brand\n  Given a user at brand A with an app password that authenticates at brand A\n  When that app password is presented to brand B\n  Then brand B does not authenticate it"
   },
   {
    "criterion_id": "01a11359-7d9c-7f40-b83a-4a935accbbc7",
    "gherkin": "@criterion-01a11359-7d9c-7f40-b83a-4a935accbbc7\nScenario: The same email at two brands is two separate users\n  Given a person registers at brand A with an email address\n  When the same person registers at brand B with the same email address\n  Then brand A and brand B each hold their own user for that email\n  And the two users have different identities"
   }
